<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nepal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nepal is a Himalayan country between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and the plains of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In the late eighteenth century the Gorkha kingdom of Nepal clashed with Tibet, prompting Qing intervention. The campaign against Nepal was counted among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qianlong-emperor">Qianlong Emperor</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ten-great-campaigns">Ten Great Campaigns</a>, which marked the furthest projection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> military power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nepal.jpg" alt="Nepal" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Biplab Anand · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_Nepal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
